# Custom Lists addon development notes

- Express ESM backend: src/server, with Node and Vercel entry points.
- Vue 3 frontend: vue/src. Shared URL parsing and list identities: shared/lists.js.
- Each user supplies their own Upstash database. Never introduce shared persistent user storage or read repository .env secrets into frontend code.
- Preserve the addon identity and existing trakt:* Redis keys. Missing provider fields mean Trakt. Cached Trakt lists must work without a Trakt API key.
- Catalog requests are Redis-only. Provider imports run separately in bounded pages and publish only a complete snapshot. Never delete a snapshot on provider failure or configuration removal.
- Connection validation must not write configuration. Keep credentials out of logs and analytics; install URLs remain sensitive credentials for compatibility.
- Use official MDBList/TMDB documentation. Do not reintroduce old JustWatch/provider or local JSON-list logic.
- Run npm test and the Vue build after changes. Tests mock network calls and never use real accounts.
